flowchart TD
  classDef works fill:#ffffff,stroke:#b8babe,color:#3a3e44;
  classDef friction fill:#f6f7f7,stroke:#3a3e44,stroke-width:2px,color:#3a3e44;
  classDef broken fill:#ffffff,stroke:#c4362b,stroke-width:2px,color:#c4362b;
  S1["1. Add (desktop) or the plus (phone) opens the<br/>save sheet, the folder preset to the last one<br/>used.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S2["2. An address typed without http, such as<br/>example.com, is refused on Save with 'Enter a<br/>full address starting with http or https.', the<br/>caret at the end of the address. The extension<br/>options try https, then http.<br/><i>friction</i>"]:::friction
  S3["3. Typing the address again removes the old error<br/>at once; the live check alone says the link is<br/>new or already saved.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S4["4. An address already saved shows 'Already saved<br/>in Homelab. Save anyway moves it here.' and the<br/>button turns into Save anyway.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S5["5. The same host on another port is a new<br/>bookmark: Not saved yet.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S6["6. Choose another folder lists every folder and<br/>New folder.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S7["7. Save closes the sheet and the card appears in<br/>its folder. No toast; screen readers hear<br/>'Saved in Homelab'.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S8["8. Bookmarklet: How to save, Computer, drag Save<br/>to Pinned into the bookmarks bar.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S9["9. On any page Save to Pinned opens /save in a<br/>small window with title, address, recent<br/>folders and Log out.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S10["10. Saving draws a tick and closes the window;<br/>where the browser keeps it open, a Saved state<br/>with Done.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S11["11. Extension: How to save, Extension: download,<br/>unzip, load unpacked; 'a token' opens API<br/>tokens. Firefox removes it when it quits, so<br/>after a restart it is loaded again with a new<br/>token.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S12["12. With a token made (flow 09), the extension<br/>options take the address and the token.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S13["13. A home address typed as most people write it,<br/>10.0.0.5:9095, tries https, then http, and Test<br/>says 'Connected to http://10.0.0.5:9095, 5<br/>folders.' An address typed with http:// for a<br/>host outside the own network first says 'On<br/>plain http your token may cross the internet<br/>unencrypted. Use https, or click Test again to<br/>connect anyway.' (Save: 'click Save again to<br/>save anyway') and goes ahead on a second click<br/>of the same button.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S14["14. With http:// Test says 'Connected, 5 folders';<br/>Save stores both and asks the browser for<br/>access to that host.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S15["15. The toolbar button or Option Shift S opens the<br/>popup: title selected, address, three recent<br/>folders, Save to Inbox.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S16["16. Saved: the tick draws and the popup closes.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S17["17. The same page again: 'Already saved in Homelab<br/>/ Network.' with Save anyway.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S18["18. On a browser page: 'This page cannot be saved'.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S19["19. The popup and options are always dark, while<br/>the app and its pages follow light and dark<br/>since 0.1.11.<br/><i>friction</i>"]:::friction
  S20["20. Right click a page or link, Save to Pinned: it<br/>goes to the Inbox and the button shows a tick,<br/>= when already saved, ! on failure.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
  S21["21. iPhone and Android: How to save shows the<br/>Safari bookmark and the home screen share<br/>target.<br/><i>works</i>"]:::works
